<http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00001060> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                  owl:versionIRI <http://model.geneontology.org/6ab067da00001060> ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/conforms_to_gpad> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                  <http://geneontology.org/lego/modelstate> "development" ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor> "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8769-177X"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/date> "2026-10-20"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title> "Regulation of GOLPH3-dependent Golgi enzyme retention (Human)"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <http://purl.org/pav/providedBy> "http://geneontology.org"^^xsd:string ;
                                                  rdfs:comment "2026-10-20: GOLPH3 cargo adaptor has_input trimmed to cargo with shown binding (B4GALT5, LYSET, GALNT7). Removed COPA, COPB1 (structure used mouse coatomer), MAN1B1, GOLIM4, FAM3C (GOLPH3-dependent levels only, binding not shown). MAN1B1 mannosidase activity unit and its indirect regulation by GOLPH3 kept."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "2026-10-20: PI4KB activity unit removed (no paper shows PI4KB acting on GOLPH3; link rested on inhibitor/yeast data). Replaced by PI4P (CHEBI:58178) 'is small molecule activator of' GOLPH3 cargo adaptor activity (IMP: Golgi PI4P depletion and PI4P-binding mutants, PMID:19837035; R90L and PIK93, PMID:42276998), PI4P located in GO:0160288 (IC)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "2026-10-20: ZDHHC13 changed from protein-cysteine S-palmitoyltransferase activity (GO:0019706, has input GOLPH3, directly positively regulates) to molecular_function (GO:0003674) causally upstream of, positive effect (RO:0002304) GOLPH3 cargo adaptor activity. ZDHHC13 has a non-canonical DQHC motif and is catalytically deficient; it promotes substrate S-acylation by a non-catalytic, unknown mechanism (PMID:42717663). Its requirement for GOLPH3 Cys-84 acylation rests on knockdown only (PMID:42276998). ZDHHC3 kept as the catalytic enzyme."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Built by claude4go 2026-09-24 as the GENERAL/regulatory layer above GOLPH3, integrating Taylor et al 2025 Sci Adv (PMID:41042862; 7.5-A cryo-ET of GOLPH3 in the COPI coat: N-terminus LVQ(R14) beta-sheet with beta-COP, folded domain on the alpha-COP beta-propeller occluding the KxKxx site, K179E/E183K abolishes retention of Golgi residents; acidic-face clusters recognise different clients), Theodoropoulou et al 2026 Nat Commun (PMID:42276998; GOLPH3 S-acylated at C84 by ZDHHC13/ZDHHC3 promoting Golgi binding and client retention, at C108/C122 by ZDHHC5 antagonising it; APT2 deacylates; NMR/ITC map LCS tail to the D247/D258/D262 acidic groove; PIK93 shows PI4KIIIbeta PI4P aids recruitment; Golph3-/- mice: GlcCer accumulation, reduced GALNT2 O-glycopeptides, partial embryonic lethality, growth and bone defects), and the client papers Rizzo 2021 (PMID:33749896), Welch 2021 (PMID:34473204), Brauer 2024 (PMID:39587297). Design: kinase and acyltransferase activities carry only the MF plus a direct regulation edge to GOLPH3 cargo adaptor activity (project convention; no acyl-CoA/PI4P molecules); GOLPH3 has_input the coat subunits COPA and COPB1 and eight representative clients; three downstream client activities represent the GSL (B4GALT5, see gomodel:6ab067da00000385), N-glycan (MAN1B1) and M6P (LYSET, see gomodel:6ab067da00000473) pathways. APT2 omitted (site and sign unknown); GALNT7/GOLIM4/FAM3C inputs only (no experimental MF in GO); mouse in vivo phenotypes left for standard mouse annotations. GOLPH3->client edges are indirect (retention/level); regulator->GOLPH3 edges are direct (covalent modification / lipid recruitment)."^^xsd:string ,
                                                               "Curated with GO AI HUB. Regulation of the GOLPH3 cargo adaptor by PI4P and by S-palmitoylation (ZDHHC3/ZDHHC13 promote, ZDHHC5 opposes), and its control of representative Golgi enzymes of three pathways (Taylor 2025, Theodoropoulou 2026)."^^xsd:string ;
                                                  <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/in_taxon> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606> .

